---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../Footer.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations, useTranslatedPath } from '../../../i18n/utils';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(lang);
const translatePath = useTranslatedPath(lang);

const KWS =
  'online speedometer, free online speedometer, online speedometer free, online speedometer test, online speedometer mph, hardspeedometer test, speedometer online train, speedometer test online, speedometer digital, gps speedometer online, my speed km/h, speedometer online, live speed test, live speedometer, zspeed, gps speedometer';

const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://instanten.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Online Speedometer', item: 'https://instanten.com/speedometer/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Contact', item: 'https://instanten.com/speedometer/contact/' },
  ],
};

---
<Layout
  title="Contact Online Speedometer — Feedback & Bug Reports"
  description="Contact the online speedometer team. Report a GPS accuracy problem with the free speedometer, suggest a feature, or ask a privacy question."
  keywords={KWS}
  ogImage="/og-image.png"
  ogImageAlt="Contact Online Speedometer — Feedback & Bug Reports"
  breadcrumbLd={breadcrumbLd}>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-[48rem] px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 lg:py-24">
    <a href={translatePath('/speedometer/')} class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-body hover:text-ink transition-colors mb-8">← Back to Speedometer</a>
    <h1 class="font-sans text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mb-2">{t('page.contact.title')}</h1>
    <p class="text-xs text-mute font-mono mb-8">Last updated: October 2026</p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
      We are a small team and we read every message. Whether you have found a bug, have a feature request, or just want to say hello — reach out using the form below.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">How the speed reading works</h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Before you write, it helps to know what the tool is doing. The <strong>online speedometer</strong>
      reads your device's GPS position through the browser and converts movement between fixes into a
      speed in km/h, mph, m/s or knots. Nothing is uploaded, which is why the
      <strong>free online speedometer</strong> keeps counting after the page has loaded even without a
      data connection.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      That design explains most support questions. A number that freezes means the GPS fix dropped, not
      that the tool stopped. A reading that starts late is normal — a
      <strong>live speed test</strong> needs the first few positions before it can calculate anything.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">Quick fixes before you write</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      <li><strong>Speed stuck at 0:</strong> allow location access when the browser asks, then reload the page.</li>
      <li><strong>Number jumps or freezes:</strong> move outdoors — buildings, trees and tunnels block GPS.</li>
      <li><strong>Reading differs from the car dash:</strong> expected; a dash is optimistic by a few percent.</li>
      <li><strong>No units you want:</strong> use the unit button for km/h, mph, m/s or knots.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">What to tell us</h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      For a bug report, tell us the phone, the browser, whether you were moving or stationary, and what
      the number showed. For an accuracy question, mention what you compared against — a dashboard, a
      bike computer or a known distance with a stopwatch — and whether you were on open road or under
      cover.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      For a feature request, describe the trip rather than the button. “I want to compare two cars on
      the same stretch” tells us more than “add a log export”, and it usually leads to a better
      <strong>speedometer digital</strong> tool.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      The questions we get most often are about units and comparison: an
      <strong>online speedometer mph</strong> reading against a km/h dial, an
      <strong>online speedometer test</strong> against a <strong>speedometer test online</strong> result
      from another site, or a <strong>speedometer online train</strong> reading that froze in a tunnel.
      Include which of those you were doing and we can usually answer in one reply.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">Email</h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@instanten.com" class="text-link hover:underline">hello@instanten.com</a>. We usually reply within a few business days.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">Send a message</h2>
    <form class="space-y-4" action="mailto:hello@instanten.com" method="post" enctype="text/plain">
      <div>
        <label for="name" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">Name</label>
        <input id="name" name="name" type="text" required class="w-full rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-link-soft focus-visible:outline-none" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">Email</label>
        <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required class="w-full rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-link-soft focus-visible:outline-none" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="subject" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">Subject</label>
        <select id="subject" name="subject" class="w-full rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-link-soft focus-visible:outline-none">
          <option>Bug report</option>
          <option>Feature request</option>
          <option>Calibration / accuracy issue</option>
          <option>Privacy question</option>
          <option>Other</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="message" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">Message</label>
        <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5" required class="w-full rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-link-soft focus-visible:outline-none"></textarea>
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-ink text-canvas px-5 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-link-soft focus-visible:outline-none">
        Send message
      </button>
    </form>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">Before you send a screenshot</h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      A screenshot helps most when it shows the unit, the trip time and the max speed together. If you
      were comparing a <strong>gps speedometer online</strong> reading with a car dial, mention both
      numbers; if you were on foot, say so, because a
      <strong>live speedometer</strong> on a walk moves in small increments and looks “stuck” to anyone
      expecting car speeds.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      People also write in after switching from an app such as <em>zspeed</em>, or after asking
      “<em>my speed km/h</em>” into a search box and landing here. Either way, the answer is the same
      <strong>online speedometer free</strong> of install — so if the number looks wrong, tell us the
      conditions and we will tell you whether it is the tool or the sky.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-sans text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mt-10 mb-4">Response times</h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      This is a small project, so replies are not instant. Accuracy reports get priority because they
      affect every user of the online speedometer; feature ideas are read and logged but may not get a
      personal reply. Privacy questions about trip data are always answered.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      While you wait, the <a href="/speedometer/blog/" class="text-link hover:underline">speedometer
      guides</a> cover the common questions about a <strong>gps speedometer</strong> reading, unit
      switching and trip resets.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>